==Czech==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|cs|zlw-ocs|vzieti}}, from {{inh|cs|sla-pro|*vъzęti}}; see {{m|cs|vz-}} and {{m|cs|jmout}}. Cognate with {{cog|ru|взять}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{audio|cs|Cs-vzít.ogg|audio}}
* {{hyphenation|cs|vzít}}

===Verb===
{{cs-verb-old|a=p|aa=brát}}

# {{lb|cs|transitive}} to [[take]] (sth {{qualifier|+ [[accusative case]]}}) (from a person {{qualifier|+ [[dative case]]}})
#: {{uxi|cs|'''Vezmu si''' [[to]].|I'll '''take''' it. (purchasing an item)}}
#: {{uxi|cs|'''Vzal''' [[mu]] [[míra|míru]].|He '''took''' his measure.}}
#: {{uxi|cs|'''Vzal''' [[mu]] [[teplota|teplotu]].|He '''took''' his temperature.}}
# {{lb|cs|transitive}} to [[take]] someone somewhere
#: {{uxi|cs|[[rodič|Rodiče]] [[mě]] '''vzali''' [[k]] [[doktor|doktorovi]].|My parents '''took''' me to a doctor.}}
# {{lb|cs|transitive}} to [[take]], to [[hold]] ('''[[za]]''' (by) + [[accusative case]])
#: {{coi|cs|vzít '''za'''...|to take '''by''' the...}}
#: {{uxi|cs|Můžu tě '''vzít za''' ruku?|May I '''hold''' your hand?}}
# {{lb|cs|reflexive|si}} to [[marry]] ''sb.'', to [[get married]] to ''sb.''
#: {{uxi|cs|Eliška '''vzala si''' Tomáše.|Eliška '''married''' Tomáš.}}

====Usage notes====
* The preposition '''za''' (behind) is used because you place your hands behinds things when you want to get a grip on them.

